{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2119","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Add or XOR"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NMiQmumW0nI"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r-906 & IA AI - Psychologic Disco"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given two non-negative integers $$$a, b$$$. You can apply two types of operations on $$$a$$$ any number of times and in any order:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$a \\gets a + 1$$$. The cost of this operation is $$$x$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$a \\gets a \\oplus 1$$$, where $$$\\oplus$$$ denotes the "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bitwise_operation#XOR"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bitwise XOR operation"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":". The cost of this operation is $$$y$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now you are asked to make $$$a = b$$$. If it's possible, output the minimum cost; otherwise, report it."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^4$$$). The description of the test cases follows. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line of each test case contains four integers $$$a, b, x, y$$$ ($$$1 \\le a, b \\le 100, 1 \\le x, y \\le 10^7$$$) — the two integers given to you and the respective costs of two types of operations."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output an integer — the minimum cost to make $$$a = b$$$, or $$$-1$$$ if it is impossible."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n7\n1 4 1 2\n1 5 2 1\n3 2 2 1\n1 3 2 1\n2 1 1 2\n3 1 1 2\n1 100 10000000 10000000\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n6\n1\n3\n-1\n-1\n990000000\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, the optimal strategy is to apply $$$a \\gets a + 1$$$ three times. The total cost is $$$1+1+1=3$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, the optimal strategy is to apply $$$a \\gets a + 1$$$, $$$a \\gets a \\oplus 1$$$, $$$a \\gets a + 1$$$, $$$a \\gets a \\oplus 1$$$ in order. The total cost is $$$2+1+2+1=6$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the fifth test case, it can be proved that there isn't a way to make $$$a = b$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"2119A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/2119/problem/A"}